text:
The reflectance package is composed of three main parts, as illustrated in Figure 1:

Configuration functions

This part contains all functions related to the configuration of the package. It allows you to define some behaviours that the functions in the ‘RS’ will automatically use. Have a look at the configuration section for more information.

Rawfiles processing functions

Functions that are used to convert the rawdata files provided by the spectrometer into interim files, i.e. standardized excel or OpenDocument files that are required to create an instance of the RS class (see following point). Have a look at the datafile section and the process rawdata files for more information.

RS class

This part contains functions embedded in the RS class and that will help you to manipulate and visualize your reflectance data. The RS class uses the data and info contained in the interim files to create visualizations or perform further computation steps.

